    {
      "key": "79997f08-333b-451d-abdb-43af70441ab7",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Which of the explorations and mini-lessons did you complete in the previous lesson?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Briefly recap the three explorations (AI as Campaign Manager; AI in Creative Writing ; and AI in Content Creation) and mini-lessons (Impact on Environment, Human Skills, and Artists) from the previous lesson.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "79997f08-333b-451d-abdb-43af70441ab7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1fdf6df8-2229-4f20-b1b5-bbadb140a24b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "82c8445b-4886-46ba-8415-e97e92bf996c",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students will meet with both expert and jigsaw groups to share findings and begin synthesizing patterns that will become actionable guidance for co-creating with AI.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students take out their Milestone 2 Learning Log from the previous lesson and their KWL Chart from Lesson 1.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Organize students into their Expert Groups based on the specific exploration they completed in the previous lesson.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Jigsaw Synthesis"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "82c8445b-4886-46ba-8415-e97e92bf996c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a208bf3f-69f5-4585-92d5-07f33bd811af"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3b3e591d-e9ce-4935-8638-49e1295e2136",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "First, meet with others who did the same exploration as you. You are the experts on that specific task.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3b3e591d-e9ce-4935-8638-49e1295e2136",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a208bf3f-69f5-4585-92d5-07f33bd811af"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d4a07a2b-f6f2-467e-911e-58dd3ada42c7",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students reflect on their experiences with the previous exploration and consider one of the following questions:\n- At what point did the product become \"mostly AI\"?\n- When did it lose your personal \"voice\" or \"values\"?\n- What human input mattered most?\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Reform groups with members from different Explorations and Mini-Lessons. Explain expectations for sharing and note-taking using the Co-Pilot Debrief organizer."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d4a07a2b-f6f2-467e-911e-58dd3ada42c7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a208bf3f-69f5-4585-92d5-07f33bd811af"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d66e08d2-0f2e-4065-b3a6-311fd44f9f80",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Now we will transition into jigsaw group. Share one finding from your Expert Group. As a group, focus on patterns and rules you found rather than just retelling the steps that you went through.",
        "remarks": true,
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students to name specific evidence (an edit, a prompt change, or a missing emotional beat) that shows where human input mattered."
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Listen for students articulating both a tipping point and a human necessity when sharing their examples."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d66e08d2-0f2e-4065-b3a6-311fd44f9f80",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a208bf3f-69f5-4585-92d5-07f33bd811af"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "95c52853-4628-4bab-8c2d-13d845d5b421",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "95c52853-4628-4bab-8c2d-13d845d5b421",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a208bf3f-69f5-4585-92d5-07f33bd811af"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "91c4fab7-ea94-4185-80d7-0e73eda64965",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students update their KWL Chart."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "91c4fab7-ea94-4185-80d7-0e73eda64965",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a208bf3f-69f5-4585-92d5-07f33bd811af"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "11d0f2a7-8401-4bee-bc52-f8f282fbbe09",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Choose one jigsaw learning from your Learning Log and write one or more responses in the KWL chart that reflects your new understanding or new questions.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "11d0f2a7-8401-4bee-bc52-f8f282fbbe09",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a208bf3f-69f5-4585-92d5-07f33bd811af"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e423e3ef-ddb5-4816-b7de-47975d36a13a",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who give very general answers and prompt them to add a specific example (for instance, a skill they'd keep vs. one they'd offload). For students who need support, offer a sentence stem from the organizer."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e423e3ef-ddb5-4816-b7de-47975d36a13a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a208bf3f-69f5-4585-92d5-07f33bd811af"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "34602efc-1c2a-4110-9df8-227a92eac732",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students apply their evidence to create clear, actionable guidelines for how they will use AI for the remainder of the course and in their final project.",
        "duration": "20",
        "name": "Project Work"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "34602efc-1c2a-4110-9df8-227a92eac732",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a208bf3f-69f5-4585-92d5-07f33bd811af"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "bfd17552-c40f-4007-895f-26139538066e",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Use your experience with your Explorations, Mini-Lessons, and your jigsaw conversations to draft a set of advice and guidelines that show how you will act as the Pilot and how you will use the AI as a Co-Pilot. Be specific: include a evidence from your testing.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "bfd17552-c40f-4007-895f-26139538066e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a208bf3f-69f5-4585-92d5-07f33bd811af"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0075644a-5db3-4053-80e0-9dd6ca926d4b",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Students draft their Co-Creation with AI guidance, making choices about medium and selecting layouts from their Digital Gallery Walk (Lesson 2).",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Push for nuance – avoid \"never\" or \"always\" statements. Ask students to cite one example from their evidence to justify each guideline."
          },
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Check that each student's draft includes a Pilot Test and an AI Impact check and that at least one guideline ties to specific evidence from their exploration."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0075644a-5db3-4053-80e0-9dd6ca926d4b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a208bf3f-69f5-4585-92d5-07f33bd811af"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "77399d9d-4771-4a4d-8b52-57927a12a531",
      "position": 12,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "77399d9d-4771-4a4d-8b52-57927a12a531",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a208bf3f-69f5-4585-92d5-07f33bd811af"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3d570c8c-9a52-4a73-85af-77f4d9915236",
      "position": 13,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 4, Level 1. Students will begin drafting the Co-Creation with AI portion of their project.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for drafts that include (a) a clear evidence from explorations and mini-lessons, (b) rules, guidance, and advice that comes from those sources, and (c) a connections to specific conversations from the jigsaw. Prompt students who miss any of these to add one concrete example or check.",
        "progression_name": "Project Work - Milestone 2"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3d570c8c-9a52-4a73-85af-77f4d9915236",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a208bf3f-69f5-4585-92d5-07f33bd811af"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "9b457a09-8fbb-42a1-945c-f2792931f5a8",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students add one new question that came up while working on the project to the Want to Know column of the KWL Chart.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who write superficial questions (for example, \"What is AI?\") and prompt them to make the question more specific (for example, \"How might AI change our community's creative work?\"). For students who are stuck, suggest they check their Co-Pilot Debrief notes for something that surprised them. For students who finish early, invite them to draft a brief action step they'd take to test their question.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Collect a quick sample of student KWL entries to check for depth—strong questions reference specific tensions (authorship, bias, skill development)."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "9b457a09-8fbb-42a1-945c-f2792931f5a8",
        "lesson_activity.key": "fb926031-198b-40c4-9e1c-f49128e09ca0"
      }
